WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.120 --> 00:00:05.160
When you see the sun rise
from the top of the world,

00:00:05.480 --> 00:00:07.480
it was just the most
beautiful thing you could imagine.

00:00:16.760 --> 00:00:20.840
My first tip would be to just start.

00:00:23.840 --> 00:00:25.640
The difference between most
successful people

00:00:25.720 --> 00:00:28.360
and unsuccessful people is that

00:00:28.440 --> 00:00:30.160
successful people
just gave it a shot,

00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:31.880
and they just took that first step.

00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:34.320
Small steps make
the biggest difference.

00:00:34.680 --> 00:00:38.280
There were so many moments,
when I've been in the Himalayas,

00:00:38.360 --> 00:00:41.080
where I've felt like
I couldn't take another step,

00:00:41.160 --> 00:00:42.800
I couldn't do anything more.

00:00:43.400 --> 00:00:48.000
And it's so easy to get paralysed
by the enormity of the challenge,

00:00:48.080 --> 00:00:50.120
and lose sight that
the step in front of you

00:00:50.200 --> 00:00:51.640
is all you have to ever worry about.

00:00:52.360 --> 00:00:54.520
My next tip: Visualise.

00:00:54.920 --> 00:00:56.920
I'd make a playlist of music

00:00:57.000 --> 00:01:00.400
that will transport me to
the mountain as soon as I put it on,

00:01:00.480 --> 00:01:03.440
shut my eyes, and I can imagine
myself climbing that peak.

00:01:03.800 --> 00:01:06.480
Just taking the time
to really visualise

00:01:06.560 --> 00:01:08.480
what it means to achieve it.

00:01:08.560 --> 00:01:09.800
I think that most people give up

00:01:09.880 --> 00:01:12.320
because they
lose sight of their dream,

00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:14.360
they forget why they started.

00:01:15.320 --> 00:01:17.280
Spend more time in nature.

00:01:17.840 --> 00:01:22.960
I always ran as a way to get fit
and I would go to the forest,

00:01:23.240 --> 00:01:25.800
the things that became
really highly emotional

00:01:25.880 --> 00:01:30.480
and I'd get really upset about
suddenly weren't such a big deal.

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:36.880
Stop letting your ego get in the way.

00:01:37.400 --> 00:01:40.960
Your ego can be the biggest wall
that you have to climb.

00:01:41.360 --> 00:01:43.000
The most successful people in life

00:01:43.080 --> 00:01:46.400
are the ones
who are able to be honest,

00:01:46.480 --> 00:01:48.640
and vulnerable with others.

00:01:48.920 --> 00:01:51.200
The more you build up
a wall around you,

00:01:51.280 --> 00:01:54.280
the more you have to pretend
to be someone that you're not.

00:01:54.720 --> 00:01:56.000
I don't think that

00:01:56.080 --> 00:01:59.960
just getting to the top of a mountain
makes you a good person,

00:02:00.240 --> 00:02:01.560
or a successful person.

00:02:02.360 --> 00:02:04.320
For me, success comes down to,

00:02:04.400 --> 00:02:09.000
can you get to that point by being
a compassionate person to others,

00:02:09.080 --> 00:02:11.440
by being in touch with yourself,

00:02:11.520 --> 00:02:14.040
and being respectful
of the environment around you.

00:02:15.560 --> 00:02:17.800
I don't believe
that you have to be ruthless

00:02:17.880 --> 00:02:19.560
to get what you want in life.

00:02:20.960 --> 00:02:25.600
My final tip is you have
to trust in something.

00:02:25.680 --> 00:02:28.760
Whether it's yourself,
whether it's in God,

00:02:28.840 --> 00:02:31.120
whether it's in nature
or the universe,

00:02:31.640 --> 00:02:35.080
but just having that trust
that it will work out somehow,

00:02:35.160 --> 00:02:37.080
and if it doesn't work
out in the way I want,

00:02:37.160 --> 00:02:39.520
then maybe I'll learn
something from it.

00:02:39.600 --> 00:02:41.320
When you have been
to the top of the world,

00:02:41.400 --> 00:02:45.160
you appreciate... such simple things,

00:02:45.240 --> 00:02:51.440
you don't want to have power
of money or status or material items.

00:02:51.520 --> 00:02:53.960
You want to have great
connections with your family,

00:02:54.040 --> 00:02:56.760
because when you think you're going
to die, they're all you think about.

00:02:57.560 --> 00:03:01.760
You want to feel that feeling when
you've been on your feet for 24 hours

00:03:01.840 --> 00:03:03.760
and you're still climbing,

00:03:03.840 --> 00:03:07.120
and you think,
"wow, the human body is amazing."

00:03:07.600 --> 00:03:12.200
Those are the moments, I think, that
have made me feel most successful,

00:03:12.280 --> 00:03:14.960
and, ultimately, those are,
in some ways,

00:03:15.320 --> 00:03:18.200
some of the hardest moments
in life to find.

